Z||000000||2xsess||01-21-2001||05:43 PM||||WEll, topic just about covers it.I'm leaving tomorrow morning, I should be back on or around the 27th. Hopefully I'll have lots of cool reading to do when I get back. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||01-21-2001||07:27 PM||||Have a good week,we'll be here when you get back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||01-21-2001||07:42 PM||||Be good, if ya can't be good be careful.<BR>Good luck.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||2birds||01-21-2001||08:51 PM||||Try not to get too dirty.||||reg||6
Z||000004||2xsess||01-21-2001||09:05 PM||||I will be careful, can't imagine what it would feel like getting run over by an M1 tank..ouch <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Thanks 2Birds, I'll try to stay clean.lol||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||01-21-2001||11:10 PM||||Hey, do you get to sleep in a tent? Just like camping. I remember getting all that good food when you're out there. You get those nice meal boxes now.<P>After 30+ years, I still remember my fisrt C rations..cold: srambled eggs and ham.  Yum yum.<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||2birds||01-22-2001||09:52 PM||||He gets paid to go camping, and I get paid to go on a cruise...<BR>We're so spoiled in today's military.||||reg||6
Z||000007||hugh||01-23-2001||07:21 AM||||Just make sure that you learn a lot on your camping trips and cruises so you can protect us better when you get back.||||reg||1
Z||000008||2xsess||01-25-2001||07:47 PM||||HEHE...I'm baaaccckkk!!<P>Yes, we get paid to go camping and get all dirty messing around with nasty tanks. No we don't sleep in tents, at leat not this time, we all slept on our vehicles. We, don't get meals in boxes though, they come in bags, they even have these cool heaters that you just add water. Of course the menu is quite varied. WE only eat those for lunch when we're in the field here at Ft Stewart though. We get "hot" chow for breakfast and dinner, it's not ever hot though. Cold runny eggs and nasty shriveled up sasuage.<BR>YUMMY    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 01-25-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||2birds||01-25-2001||10:30 PM||||Submarines get the best food in the Navy.  <BR>We get cool things like <BR>1. Lizard Eggs (canned new potatoes, cooked in all kinds of imaginative ways)<BR>2. Elephant Scabs (Breaded Veal patties)<BR>3. Chicken Wheels (self-explanatory)<BR>4. Pus Rockets (Italian Sausages with "natural casings")  Be careful where you sit when the guy across from you tries to stab his with a fork.<P>Sometimes I think having an operational Deep Fat Fryer is a requirement to dive the ship.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||2birds||01-25-2001||10:35 PM||||Sorry, I almost forgot Baboon Ass, aka Corned Beef.<P>Welcome back to the world, 2xsess.  Just in time for a nice warm weekend. ||||reg||10
Z||000011||2xsess||01-26-2001||10:33 PM||||Ya know, I noticed something, the whole time I was out there it like never got above 50 degrees and now next week it's supposed to be like in the high 60s to low 70s...does mother nature hate the military too?<P>Interesting menu there 2Birds<P>We only get cool things like<P>Track pads aka MRE Fudge Brownies.<BR>(for those of you that don't know these are the rubber squares on the track) Some of the dryest umm food you'll ever eat.<P>Chicken Spew - MRE Chicken Stew..kind of looks like someone already ate it once.<P>Beef Spew...see above<P>Donkey D---s....MRE Frankfuters..don't taste like any frankfuters I've ever eaten before.<P>Hockey pucks....sausages so hard you break your plastic knife trying to cut.<P>Oh and the lovely MRE crackers that are in every meal, the big challenge in Basic was to see who could actually eat both of them without taking a drink. They're like eating sawdust.<P>But, the guys that eat at the Dining facilities on post actually get it pretty good, every Thursday is Steak and Lobster for dinner. Of course I can't really saw what the steak looks like but le me put it this way, it doesn't look like part of a cow, just something that the cow left <I>behind</I>. And about as tough as plywood.<P>Hey 2birds, do they teach the Navy cooks the imfamous ChiliMac too? If they do you'll know what I'm talking about.hehe<BR>||||reg||1
